<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 26 July, from 657 to 1956.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muawiya-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">657 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,369 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The armies of Ali and Muawiya meet at Siffin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Siffin on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib">Ali ibn Abi Talib</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiya</a>, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. As Ali's army began to gain the upper hand, the Syrians called for arbitration, which divided Ali's supporters and led to the secession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharijites">Kharijites</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-siffin">Battle of Siffin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib">Ali ibn Abi Talib</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiya I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">811 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,215 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Nikephoros I falls in battle against Khan Krum's Bulgarians</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> had burned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliska">Pliska</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krum">Khan Krum</a>'s forces trapped their army in a pass of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a> and destroyed almost all of it. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-i">Emperor Nikephoros</a> I was killed and his heir Staurakios seriously wounded.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-i">Nikephoros I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">920 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abd al-Rahman III defeats León and Pamplona at Valdejunquera</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> defeated the combined forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ordono-ii-of-leon">Ordoño II of León</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-garces-i-of-pamplona">Sancho Garcés I of Pamplona</a>, capturing several leading men. The Umayyad state went on to sack <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> in 924.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-valdejunquera">Battle of Valdejunquera</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1581">1581 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">445 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dutch provinces renounce Philip II in the Act of Abjuration</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The States General of the rebel provinces declared that Philip II had forfeited his rule by tyranny. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-abjuration">Act of Abjuration</a> was in effect a declaration of independence for what became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-abjuration">Act of Abjuration</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1745">1745 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">281 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First recorded women's cricket match is played in Surrey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eleven women of Bramley played eleven of Hambledon on Gosden Common near Guildford, reported in the Reading Mercury. It is the earliest recorded women's cricket match.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1847">1847 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Liberia declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Liberia, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society">American Colonization Society</a> as a home for freed Black Americans, declared itself an independent republic. It became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>'s oldest modern republic, though settler rule marginalised indigenous peoples.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1908">1908 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">118 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bureau of Investigation, forerunner of the FBI, is created</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Attorney General Charles Bonaparte set up a force of special agents in the US Justice <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>. Renamed the FBI in 1935, it grew under J. Edgar Hoover into America's main federal police agency.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fidel Castro leads the attack on the Moncada Barracks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a> led some 160 rebels against the Moncada Barracks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>. The attack failed, but his trial speech 'History Will Absolve Me' made him a national figure, and 26 July named his movement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1956">1956 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nasser nationalises the Suez Canal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Nasser</a> announced the nationalisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> Company to fund the Aswan Dam. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Israel invaded in October, but US pressure forced a humiliating withdrawal.</p></div></li></ol>
